# Known-flaky or expected-missing URLs to exclude from link checking.
# One pattern per line; supports regex.

# Placeholder/example URLs
https?://example\.com
https?://localhost

# CDN resources (may rate-limit CI)
https://cdnjs\.cloudflare\.com

# Links pinned to a commit of the repository (GitHub rate-limits the checker; the build checks the files exist)
https://github\.com/corvus-dotnet/Corvus\.Regex\.Ecma262/blob/

# The package page exists once the first release is published
https://www\.nuget\.org/packages/Corvus\.Regex\.Ecma262

# The site's own absolute URLs (canonical links, the sitemap): not there until the site is deployed, and checked as root-relative links anyway
https://corvus-oss\.org/Corvus\.Regex\.Ecma262
# The daily benchmark run is written to gh-pages by the benchmarks workflow and is never in the site build output.
benchmarks/ci/
